{"question_id": "q04", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Based on the corpus, two approaches let an assistant recall old notes without a huge context window:\n\n**1. Long-term memory with paging (MemGPT).** A memory store retains past notes across sessions. When needed, it ranks and retrieves only the relevant ones, paging them into a small context window [S1].\n\n**2. Fixed-size state memory (state space models).** A state space model scans the sequence while maintaining a fixed-size memory, giving linear cost and strong long-range recall without expanding the context [S6].\n\nBoth are vetted preprints.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dec-01", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "nm-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 5042, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
