{"question_id": "q06", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "**Why plan steps before acting:** Planning breaks a goal into ordered steps before any action is taken [S1]. This decomposition allows the planner to revise the list when a step fails [S1].\n\n**Who checks the outcome:** A verifier checks the outcome [S1]. In browser automation contexts, systems like PilotEval grade tasks step by step [S3].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "nm-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 6951, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q07", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Based on the available corpus, self-correction works (i.e., produces gains) **only when the critic is grounded in a checkable signal** [S1]. The source describes self-correction as a process where a system critiques its own answer and tries again, but emphasizes that improvements appear exclusively under this condition.\n\n*Source reliability: vetted_preprint (a preprint with a quality signal, not peer-reviewed).*", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-10", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "nm-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S12", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 7454, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q08", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Based on the available sources, a **token budget** mechanism stops spending once a run reaches its predefined cap [S1]. The system uses tools that measure the cost in real time, and the agent responds accordingly to enforce the limit [S2]. Another system, LedgerGuard, is designed to detect and flag runs that do exceed their budget, providing a monitoring layer [S3].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "nm-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ml-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-13", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item", "get_item", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 8076, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q09", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Before a dangerous (risky) step runs in a workflow, a human-in-the-loop review pauses the workflow and the reviewer sees the proposed action and its evidence; the workflow resumes only after approval [S7].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 4734, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q10", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "According to a peer-reviewed source, long-horizon tasks that require hundreds of sequential steps fail primarily due to **error accumulation** and **context limits** [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dec-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 4818, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q11", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Based on the corpus, telemetry in the form of **tracing and observability** shows where a program gets stuck or loops. Specifically, traces record every model call, tool call, and latency as a span, and these traces **expose where a run stalled or looped** [S11].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "af-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 7935, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q12", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Defending against hidden instructions in web pages (prompt injection) is addressed by **labeling untrusted content and refusing to follow any instructions found inside it** [S1]. This peer-reviewed work describes the threat as prompt injection that hides instructions in a web page or document the model later reads, and the defense as explicitly marking such content as untrusted so the model will not execute embedded commands.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "af-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 4867, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q13", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Based on the available source, deepfake speech detection must generalize to voices it never trained on, and the key approach to improving this generalization is using **front-end features and augmentation to reduce the \"speaker shortcut\"**\u2014i.e., preventing the model from relying on speaker-specific cues rather than spoofing artifacts [S1].  \n\nThe source is a vetted preprint (not peer-reviewed) and provides only this high-level summary; no further technical details (e.g., specific feature types, augmentation strategies, or benchmark results) are available in the corpus.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "nm-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S12", "external_id": "af-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 9842, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q14", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "**Sparse attention** reduces the quadratic cost of full attention by attending only to a subset of positions for each query; routing mechanisms select the keys that matter most [S2].\n\n**State space models (SSMs)** replace attention entirely with a recurrent scan that maintains a fixed-size memory, yielding linear cost in sequence length while preserving long-range recall [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 4999, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q15", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "**Mixture-of-experts (MoE) routing** replaces the dense feed-forward sub-layers in each transformer block with a set of expert feed-forward networks. For each token, a learned router selects only a few experts to activate, reducing computation while increasing model capacity. The router is trained to balance load across experts and maintain quality [S1].\n\n**Rotary positional encodings (RoPE)** change how position information is added to the transformer. Instead of adding separate positional embeddings to token representations, RoPE injects position by rotating the query and key vectors in attention. This rotation-based approach allows the model to generalize to longer sequences by scaling the rotation frequencies [S10].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ml-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ml-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-13", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-10", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "ml-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S12", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 10356, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q16", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "**Text watermarking** (S2) embeds a traceable signal *during generation* by biasing token choices with a secret key, so a detector can later recover the signal and establish provenance of machine-written text.\n\n**Attacking an image watermark** (S3) is an *adversarial, post-hoc process*: an attacker perturbs a generated image (e.g., adds noise, crops, compresses) until the watermark detector fails to detect the embedded signal. Robustness is measured against such perturbations.\n\nIn short, text watermarking is a **proactive provenance mechanism** applied at generation time on discrete tokens, while attacking an image watermark is a **reactive evasion technique** applied to continuous pixel data to defeat detection. [S2, S3]", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "af-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "nm-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "dec-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 5123, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
